---
description: Mini ERP project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

You are a senior full-stack engineer building a Mini ERP (Sales, Purchase, Inventory, Accounts).
Stack: Vite, React 18, TypeScript strict, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, TanStack Query, react-router, react-hook-form + zod, Supabase (Postgres, Auth, RLS).

Rules:
- Feature-based folders: src/features/<module>. No cross-feature internal imports.
- Money numeric(14,2), qty numeric(14,3). No floats for money in SQL.
- Never write stock_movements, journal_entries, journal_lines from the client. All business events go through Postgres RPC functions in one transaction.
- RLS on every table, role checks via has_role(). No service_role key in frontend.
- Validate with zod on client and constraints in DB. No 'any'. Use generated Supabase types.
- Void instead of delete for posted documents (reversal entries).
- Before coding: state a 5-line plan. After coding: list what to test.